<h2>Quick Reference Card</h2>
<p>A cheat sheet that groups the commands you use often by situation. Handy for finding something quickly while working.</p>

<h3>Getting started</h3>
<ul>
    <li><code>/deepinit</code> — document the project structure</li>
    <li><code>/deep-interview</code> — clarify requirements</li>
    <li><code>/omc-doctor</code> — diagnose the installation</li>
</ul>

<h3>Planning</h3>
<ul>
    <li><code>/plan</code> — draw up a plan, then approve it (omc-plan)</li>
    <li><code>ralplan:</code> — planning based on expert consensus</li>
</ul>

<h3>Execution (in order of intensity)</h3>
<ul>
    <li><code>autopilot:</code> — autonomous execution (planning to verification)</li>
    <li><code>ralph:</code> — repeat until done</li>
    <li><code>ulw</code> — maximum parallel execution</li>
    <li><code>team N:agent</code> — team collaboration with N agents</li>
</ul>

<h3>Analysis &amp; review</h3>
<ul>
    <li><code>deep-analyze</code> — debugging · root-cause analysis</li>
    <li><code>review code</code> — comprehensive code review</li>
    <li><code>security review</code> — check for security vulnerabilities</li>
    <li><code>fix build</code> — fix build · type errors</li>
    <li><code>tdd:</code> — test-driven development</li>
</ul>

<h3>Multi-AI</h3>
<ul>
    <li><code>/omc-teams N:ai</code> — use Codex · Gemini in parallel</li>
    <li><code>/ccg</code> — analysis by 3 models at once</li>
</ul>

<h3>Utilities</h3>
<ul>
    <li><code>/cancel</code> — cancel the current mode</li>
    <li><code>/cancel --force</code> — reset everything</li>
    <li><code>/trace</code> — evidence-based root-cause tracking</li>
    <li><code>skillify</code> — extract · reuse patterns (formerly learner)</li>
    <li><code>/hud setup</code> — install the status line (HUD)</li>
</ul>

<div class="note">
    <span class="nh">At a glance</span>
    Mode intensity: conversation &lt; plan &lt; autopilot &lt; ralph &lt; team ralph · model cost: haiku &lt; sonnet &lt; opus
</div>
